{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776895670,"nonce":"GVwILos9ztQTi8EXgIW7dHEEWaY=","title":"Container exits with .git pointer set to container paths, breaks host git","message":"## Problem\nWhen the container exits, the worktree's .git file still points to container paths (/repo-git/worktrees/...) instead of host paths. This breaks host-side git operations, pre-review rebase, and causes orphan detection loops.\n\n## Root cause\ndocker-entrypoint.sh rewrites .git for container use but doesn't restore on exit.\n\n## Proposed Solution\nWatcher restores .git pointer after container exits.\n\n## Files\n- host/watcher/session_monitor.py\n\n## Tests\n- tests/test_worktree_git_fix.py::test_git_pointer_restored_after_container_exit\n\nREQ: REQ-003","files":null}]}